      "description": "Watch St. Louis City II vs Colorado Rapids highlights and goals from Major League Soccer on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 26, 2026. On July 26, 2026, St. Louis City II hosted Colorado Rapids in an MLS encounter that would be defined by a massive shift in momentum during the opening stages. Both teams entered the pitch with high energy, but the strategic landscape was altered almost immediately. Early Dismissal Reshapes the Game The defining moment of the first half arrived in the 12th minute when Rob Holding was shown a straight red card. The decision sparked heavy protests from the Colorado Rapids players, but the referee remained firm, leaving the visitors with ten men for the remainder of the contest. To compensate for the loss, Colorado sacrificed Dante Sealy for Miguel Navarro in a defensive tactical switch. As the half progressed, the match turned into a gritty battle of attrition. St. Louis City II pushed forward to exploit their man advantage, but the visitors remained disciplined despite yellow cards for Hamzat Ojediran and Christopher Durkin . Despite the sustained pressure from the home side, the two teams headed into the locker rooms at halftime with the score still level at 0-0. Ostrak Delivers the Final Blow The second half saw a flurry of substitutions as both managers looked to break the deadlock. The decisive move came in the 76th minute when Tomas Ostrak was introduced in place of Durkin . It took only seven minutes for the substitute to make his mark. In the 83rd minute, Tomas Totland provided a pinpoint assist, allowing Tomas Ostrak to find the back of the net and put St. Louis City II ahead. Colorado tried to fight back in the closing stages, but their efforts were hampered by fatigue and the numerical disadvantage. A late yellow card for Kosi Thompson in stoppage time highlighted the frustration of the visitors. When the referee blew the final whistle after seven minutes of added time, St. Louis City II walked away with a hard-earned 1-0 victory, rewarding their patience and tactical execution."
